- op: discuss  # 0bfb
  at: '2026-02-25T08:13:51Z'  # 0bfb
  by: human  # 0bfb
  actor: jgstern  # 0bfb
  clock: 3  # 0bfb
  nonce: 0bfb  # 0bfb
  message: "- (a) Name-based + caller-file-span threshold — quickest, catches the obvious cases (log, warn, error, debug, info, trace, fatal). Fragile against custom logger wrappers.\n  - (b) Behavioral detection — most principled (high in-degree + low semantic diversity). But risks false positives on legitimate hub functions.\n  - (c) Framework-aware tagging — most robust (logrus, zap, slog, log4j, winston, structlog as YAML patterns with infrastructure:logging category). Requires maintaining YAML entries per logging library but fits the existing framework pattern\n  system.\n\nLet's go with (a)+(c) as it is the pragmatic combination — name-based catches universal patterns, framework YAML catches library-specific ones."  # 0bfb
